# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q -l .chktexrc statement.tex
#
# Two warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 23 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, each with a 100% false-positive rate here:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with braces." Fires on
#       $(\Msp')^{k}$ and $(\Msp')^{k'}$, where the superscript attaches to
#       the parenthesised message space exactly as intended -- the group is
#       the object being raised to a power, and adding braces around the
#       parenthesis would change nothing but the source.
#   36  "You should put a space after parenthesis." Fires once, inside the
#       bibliography, on the title "Three's compromised too: Circular
#       insecurity for any cycle length from (ring-)LWE", which is copied
#       exactly as the source paper's own reference list prints it. Adding
#       the space chktex wants would misquote the title.
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 23 August 2026 the file is clean under
# this config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n36
}
